    { icon: "🇦🇺", t: "Australia lost its second leg: copper fell another 2.33% and is down 15.91% on the month", s: "Yesterday it was employment minus 43,500 against a plus 25,500 forecast with unemployment at a four-year high of 4.9%. Today it is the China and industrial-demand leg, with copper at 5.4989. Core inflation 3.6% and headline 4.3% against a 4.85% cash rate still leave the board unable to hike or cut, and TradingEconomics carries 4.85% for December 8. AUD/JPY and AUD/NZD are the expressions; AUD/USD comes down to medium on the dollar leg." },
    { icon: "🛢️", t: "Day 264 of a closed strait and WTI is 82.51, down 14.92% on the month - still no premium at all", s: "Iran’s army said on November 19 that three oil tankers struck naval mines and caught fire in the eastern Strait of Hormuz, and a British monitor confirmed one vessel hit by an unknown projectile; the Revolutionary Guard separately claimed two supertankers. IMF PortWatch logged two transits on November 15 against a pre-crisis baseline near 85 a day. WTI is plus 0.26% and Brent 92.18 and plus 0.23%. The asymmetry is still up and the trend still down, so USOIL stays a range." }
